FILE: assets/css/modalDisplayer.css
FEATURE: modal-displayer-verification
DATE: 2026-08-03

================================================================================
CHANGE 1 — Define the .xScroll overlay rule
================================================================================

OLD_SECTION
.vModal{
  position:fixed;
  top:0;
  width:100%;
  height:100vh;
  z-index:999;
  display:none;
  min-width:320px;
}

NEW_SECTION
.vModal{
  position:fixed;
  top:0;
  width:100%;
  height:100vh;
  z-index:999;
  display:none;
  min-width:320px;
}
/* the page body is frozen while a modal is open, so a modal taller
   than the viewport has to scroll inside the overlay itself */
.vModal.xScroll{
  overflow-y:auto;
  overflow-x:hidden;
}

REASON
`createElements()` in vUX-modalDisplayer.js has always added the class `xScroll` to
the overlay alongside `vModal`, but that class was defined in no stylesheet in the
repository (grep across assets/css/*.css returned nothing), so it was inert.

The consequence was a functional bug rather than a cosmetic one. While a modal is
open the module sets `body { position: fixed }` to stop the page behind from
scrolling. The overlay is `position: fixed; height: 100vh` with default
`overflow: visible`. A modal taller than the viewport therefore overflowed the
overlay with no scroll container anywhere: the body could not scroll because it was
frozen, and the overlay would not scroll because it had no overflow rule. Everything
past the first viewport-height of a tall modal was unreachable — the user could not
scroll to a submit button at the bottom of a long form.

Defining `.xScroll` with `overflow-y: auto` makes the overlay the scroll container,
which is what the class name always implied and what the pinned-to-top positioning
in `positionVertically()` (CHANGE 3 of the JS log) assumes. `overflow-x: hidden`
prevents a stray horizontal scrollbar from the `translateX(-50%)` centring used on
`.modalSpace`. Verified by the "tall modal is scrollable inside the overlay" and
"tall modal bottom reachable" checks.
